  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q35-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "When $P(x)=x^3+2x^2+ax+b$ is divided by $x^2+2x-3$, the remainder is $4x+3$. Find $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p8-q35-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=1,\\quad b=3",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p8-q35-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=-3",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " into the division transformation and solve simultaneously.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "By the division transformation,\n\n$$P(x)=(x^2+2x-3)Q(x)+4x+3.$$\n\nSince $x^2+2x-3=(x-1)(x+3)$, substitute $x=1$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1+2+a+b&=4+3\\\\a+b&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $x=-3$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-27+18-3a+b&=-12+3\\\\-3a+b&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtract the second equation from the first:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(a+b)-(-3a+b)&=4-0\\\\4a&=4\\\\a&=1\\\\b&=4-1\\\\b&=3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
